    solid-memo:front "A team believes the Standard requires its codebase to be used by several organizations already. What level does Make the codebase reusable and portable actually set for that?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "SHOULD: use by multiple parties is recommended"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "The criterion requires the codebase to be developed for reuse in different contexts; actual use by multiple parties, a shared roadmap and shared development are SHOULDs."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-reusable-3b-d1> ,
                          <#q-reusable-3b-d2> ,
                          <#q-reusable-3b-d3> .

<#q-reusable-3b-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "MUST: use by multiple parties is required"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "The MUST is to be developed for reuse; actual use by multiple parties is a SHOULD."@en .

<#q-reusable-3b-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "OPTIONAL: use by multiple parties is a bonus"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "It is a SHOULD, not OPTIONAL: it may be set aside only for a valid reason whose full implications have been weighed."@en .

<#q-reusable-3b-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "SHOULD NOT: use by multiple parties is discouraged"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "The criterion encourages more parties, not fewer: use, roadmap and development by multiple parties are all SHOULDs."@en .

<#q-reusable-r01>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
